Well, your sense of "interest" is not what I take
to be the ordinary sense: "find interesting"
roughly.  It has nothing to do with pleasure or
not of the subject and always at least implicates
pleasure in knowing more about the subject,
however repulsive it may be.  And in that sense,
there is no middle ground: I am interested or
not.  The other reading of {a'unai}, "interested
in the opposite of the subject" also doesn't seem
to fit very well, but at least on that spectrum
there is a middle ground: don't care about either
of them (but notice that the two extremes are
then not exclusive: I can be interested in both A
and not-A).

